---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

title: "Roadmap";
description: "High‑level roadmap for the Umi‑Time project.";
---

<Base title="Roadmap">
  <div class="umi-region umi-pad">
    <main class="page page-roadmap">
      <header class="page-header">
        <h1>Roadmap</h1>
        <p>
          This page outlines the long‑term direction of the Umi‑Time project.
          The roadmap is intentionally high‑level and will evolve as the standard,
          the core library, and the website grow.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Placeholder Roadmap -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>Upcoming Milestones</h2>
        <p>
          The detailed roadmap will be added here. It will include planned work
          across the core library (<code>umi-time-js</code>), the documentation site,
          solar geometry modules, formatting specifications, and future demos.
        </p>

        <p>
          For now, this section serves as a placeholder. You can edit it directly
          in <code>www/src/pages/roadmap.astro</code> when you're ready to define
          the next phases of the project.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Project Philosophy -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>Project Philosophy</h2>
        <p>
          Umi‑Time aims to be a precise, transparent, and accessible standard for
          solar‑aligned timekeeping. The roadmap will reflect this philosophy by
          prioritizing correctness, clarity, and practical usefulness.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Versioning -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>Versioning</h2>
        <p>
          Major roadmap milestones will align with semantic versioning of the
          <code>umi-time</code> npm package. Breaking changes will be documented
          clearly, and new features will be introduced in minor releases.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Feedback -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>Feedback & Suggestions</h2>
        <p>
          If you have ideas for the roadmap or want to propose a direction for
          future development, please open an issue on GitHub or contribute through
          the <a href="/contributing">Contributing</a> page.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</Base>
